From c9c8372ce5d32763b97b0bed253b7b0b7eb47ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:45:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 download history follow-up: archived rows on
 demand, a drain budget and a cheaper download start

Archived rows (tab/067) were invisible to Chromium's own surfaces:
chrome://downloads and the downloads extension API saw only live items, so
downloads.search's documented startedAfter paging, limit 0, erase and an ID
from an earlier session missed every row past the newest 5,000.
DownloadHistory::RestoreArchivedRows reads the rows again from the History
DB (archived rows keep a summary only), keeps those still archived and
creates them as items newest first, in the initial load's 8 ms slices; the
live limit is then lifted for the session and on_loaded runs again. Rows
removed while it runs are not restored; one already made an item is removed
as an item. DownloadsUI::CreatePageHandler and every downloads extension
function but download() restore first; a function waits (RespondLater) and
fails as a queued function does if the history goes away.
DownloadsListTracker::InsertItem walks only as far as the rows the page
holds: a full std::distance per created item made a restore under an open
page quadratic (~9 s at 39,413 rows).

Every download's start drew Chromium's Dock tile in the download's own task
(the app icon's lookup and image, and an NSNumberFormatter per draw that
loaded the system ICU's locale data). The tile is now drawn one DockIcon
period (5 Hz) later, coalesced, and its count uses base::FormatNumber.
CancelAllEphemeralWarnings, run when the history load completes, skips
complete items (Cancel is a no-op for them) before building a
DownloadItemModel for each.

The bridge delivers host callbacks for at most 8 ms per task; a longer burst
continues in the next task, in order. The flush after ChromeMain returns is
not budgeted.

Bridge 0.51.0. No ABI change: ABI 1.48 layouts and functions are unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-07 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
